1. Executive Summary
ASM Social is a next-generation social network built around digital avatars, not personal profiles. The platform enables users to find and interact with others based on similar body parameters, clothing fit, and style preferences, creating a trusted environment for communication, group purchases, exchanges, and resale.
Unlike traditional social networks, ASM Social focuses not on user identity or attention, but on objective, utility-driven avatar data, ensuring privacy, accuracy, and tangible value.

2. The Problem
2.1 Social Networks Do Not Solve Practical Problems
Modern social platforms:
are built around identity and attention;
encourage comparison rather than meaningful interaction;
lack tools for trusted decision-making in e-commerce.
2.2 Online Shopping Lacks Social Trust
Users:
do not know how an item will actually fit;
do not trust reviews from random people;
frequently return products, increasing costs for everyone.


3. The Solution: ASM Social
ASM Social is an avatar-based social network where:
users interact through Avatar ID;
recommendations are based on real body and style compatibility;
social connections generate real economic value.
People don’t just “follow” each other — they match by body and taste.

4. Core Concept
4.1 Avatar-First Social Graph
At the center of the system is a digital avatar that includes:
body size matrix (ASM);
body proportions;
clothing fit history (fit feedback);
style preferences.
The social graph is built between avatars, not between real-world identities.

5. Key Features of ASM Social
5.1 Avatar Matching
The platform calculates an Avatar Similarity Score based on:
size and proportions;
confirmed successful clothing fits;
style and price preferences.
Users see:
avatars with high compatibility (e.g., 90%+);
items that “fit well” on similar avatars.

5.2 Style-Based Social Feed
Personalized feeds such as:
“Fits best on avatars like yours”
“People with similar style are buying”
“Verified successful fits”
No influencers. No likes. Only relevance.

5.3 Social Commerce
ASM Social enables:
group buying;
pre-orders and drops for avatar-based groups;
exchange and resale between compatible avatars;
“Will this fit me?” requests to a trusted cluster.

5.4 Reputation & Trust Layer
Each avatar has:
a Fit Reputation Score;
a history of verified recommendations;
trust based on data, not popularity.
User identity remains private.


6. Privacy and Anonymity
ASM Social is designed as a privacy-first platform:
no real names or photos;
separation of Avatar ID and real identity;
full user control over data visibility;
compliance with GDPR and privacy-by-design principles.

7. Users and Ecosystem
7.1 Users
receive accurate recommendations;
save time and money;
find people truly similar to them.
7.2 Brands
work with anonymous avatar clusters;
reduce returns;
launch collections based on real body data.
7.3 The Platform
benefits from strong network effects;
accumulates high-quality data;
scales without sacrificing trust.

8. Growth Loop
User creates an avatar
Finds similar avatars
Receives accurate recommendations
Makes a successful purchase
Confirms fit
Increases network value
Each new user strengthens the entire system.

9. Business Model (High-Level)
B2B partnerships with brands and retailers
Social commerce commissions
Premium features for users
White-label solutions for platforms
ASM Social does not sell attention — it sells accuracy and trust.

10. Vision
ASM Social is a social infrastructure for digital bodies and taste.
A world where recommendations work, privacy is preserved, and social connections have real value.



11. Conclusion
ASM Social redefines what a social network can be: from a platform of self-presentation to a platform of meaningful interaction.
It is a social network:
not of people, but of avatars;
not of attention, but of compatibility;
not of noise, but of trust.
